  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6Zt8F_",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3794467783,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Loyalty.Customer/Application/Commands/Enrolment/BasicCustomerCommandHandler.cs",
      "line": 115,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3794467783",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The condition `preferredEmail?.Valid != \"N\"` will evaluate to `true` when `preferredEmail` is null (because null != \"N\"), causing email triggering even when there is no preferred email. Update the guard to require a preferred email exists and is not marked invalid (e.g., check `preferredEmail != null` and compare `Valid` explicitly, ideally case-insensitively / via existing string helpers).",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Fixed the null guard so email publication requires an actual preferred email, and used the repository's case-insensitive Is extension when checking the Valid flag."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6Zt8Gd",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3794467821,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Loyalty.Enrolment/Mapper/CreateCustomerEventEntitiesMapper.cs",
      "line": 62,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3794467821",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "Using `ToLower()` is culture-sensitive and can produce unexpected results in some locales (e.g., Turkish-i). Prefer `ToLowerInvariant()` for normalizing email addresses (same applies to other mappers doing the same normalization).",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Replaced ToLower() with ToLowerInvariant() for culture-independent email normalization."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6Zt8Gu",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3794467843,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Loyalty.Customer/Mapper/Enrolment/CreateEnrolCustomerCommandMapper.cs",
      "line": 64,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3794467843",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "Same as above: `ToLower()` is culture-sensitive; use `ToLowerInvariant()` when normalizing email addresses to avoid locale-dependent behavior.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Replaced ToLower() with ToLowerInvariant() for culture-independent email normalization."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6Zt8G-",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3794467861,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Mutations/CreateUnder18AccountMutation.cs",
      "line": 41,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3794467861",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The condition `claims?.CustomerId.IsNullOrWhiteSpace() != false` is hard to read and easy to misunderstand. Consider rewriting this into clearer, direct checks (e.g., explicitly check `claims is null` and then check required fields) so future changes don't accidentally weaken the validation logic.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Rewrote the condition as explicit claims-null and required-identifier checks while retaining the repository string extensions."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6Zt8HO",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3794467882,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Mutations/CreateUnder18AccountMutation.cs",
      "line": 87,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3794467882",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`HouseHoldLinking` returns a `ResponseMessage`, but the mutation discards it and always returns the enrolment response. If `HouseHoldLinking` can fail without throwing, this mutation could report success even when the household link did not occur. Either (a) use the returned `ResponseMessage` to detect/report link failures, or (b) change the provider API to return `Task` if the only valid behavior is “throw on failure”.",
      "decision": "invalid",
      "resolutionComment": "No code change. HouseHoldMutationProvider uses the shared HttpConnector, whose SendAsync throws HttpRequestException for every non-success HTTP status before returning. The ResponseMessage contract has only a Message string and exposes no status or error code that the mutation could reliably inspect."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6Zt8HY",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3794467897,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Mutations/CreateUnder18AccountMutation.cs",
      "line": 62,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3794467897",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "This mutation introduces several new branches and failure modes (missing/invalid token, parent resolution failure, DOB/age boundary, enrolment returning no member/customer ID). The PR adds a factory unit test and an end-to-end automation test, but the mutation itself would benefit from unit/transport tests in `VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account.Tests` to validate these branches deterministically (without relying on downstream services or timing).",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Added focused mutation unit tests for missing access token, unresolved parent claims, and the under-18 age boundary using handwritten dependency stubs, plus retained the existing factory and end-to-end coverage."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6ZvtBq",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3795133767,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Services/Under18AccountRequestFactory.cs",
      "line": 32,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3795133767",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`parent.AddressDetails?.Select(...).ToList()` can throw a `NullReferenceException` when `parent.AddressDetails` is null because `.ToList()` is invoked via a non-null-conditional call on a potentially-null sequence. Make the entire chain null-safe (e.g., apply the null-conditional operator to `ToList()` as well, or coalesce `parent.AddressDetails` to an empty sequence before `Select`) so missing parent addresses do not crash the U18 factory.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Made missing parent addresses produce an empty child address list and added a focused factory regression test."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6Zv6Vi",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3795212274,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Mutations/CreateUnder18AccountMutation.cs",
      "line": 87,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3795212274",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The mutation does not validate the result of `HouseHoldLinking(...)` (it awaits the call but ignores the returned `ResponseMessage`). If the downstream call returns a non-OK response without throwing, the mutation will still return a successful enrolment response even though household linking failed. Capture the response and fail the mutation when the link response indicates an error (e.g., status not OK / error code present), so the client gets a deterministic failure and retries don’t silently create partially-linked state.",
      "decision": "invalid",
      "resolutionComment": "Duplicate of the household-linking comment above. The shared HttpConnector throws for non-success HTTP responses, and ResponseMessage contains no machine-readable status or error field to validate after a successful HTTP call."
    }
  ],
